blazing fast duplicate detector written in 135 lines of C code

FEAUTRES
- doesn't remove the files, instead prints output which can be piped into a shell "rm duplicate-file # file"
- skips symbolic links
- skips blank files

ALGORITHM
- scan a file
- if it's size is unique then add it to the scanned files and stop
otherwise
- set n = 4096
- compare n bytes of both files if they differ then stop
- set n = n * 3 and continue by checking the next n bytes of each file, if they differ then stop
- if all bytes are exhauseted then the files are duplicates

depends on uthash

$ find ~/dir -type f | wc -l
6282
$ time duplicate ~/dir >/dev/null
real	0m 0.06s
user	0m 0.00s
sys	0m 0.05s
